# DTF tier manifest: composer-virtual-packagist-member  (artifact-keeper#4951)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-scan-formats (its Packagist-shaped
# Composer upstream: p2/<vendor>/<pkg>.json whose dist.url points at a
# separate /composer/zipball/<pkg>.zip endpoint) + client.composer (a real
# Composer 2 client on the DTF network only, so it can reach the backend but
# not the mock).
#
# #4951: a Composer Virtual over a non-scanning Remote member pointing at a
# Packagist-style upstream answered 404 for the dist the Remote serves, because
# the virtual walk synthesized dist/<vendor>/<pkg>/<version>/<ref>.zip against
# the member's upstream base. The virtual p2 metadata also passed the member's
# dist.url through verbatim, so clients bypassed the Virtual entirely.
#
# Red on 1.11.7 (and 1.12.0 main before the fix); green with the fix.
#
# #6285: search.json on a Composer Virtual searched only the Virtual's own
# (always empty) artifact rows, so a package published to a hosted member was
# installable through the Virtual but never found by its search.json. A third
# Virtual over a Local and the Remote must find the Local's package. Red on
# main before the fix (artifact-keeper 1.12.4).
#
# #6332: search.json forwarded to a Remote's upstream, opt-in per Remote
# (composer_upstream_search). On: the upstream's package is found through the
# Remote. Off (the default): the upstream is never asked. Five identical
# searches cost one upstream read. A Virtual over a Local and an opted-in
# Remote whose upstream answers 503 returns the Local's package with 200 and
# names the Remote in X-AK-Partial-Members. The setting is refused (400) on
# an npm Remote and a Composer Local. A Virtual over an opted-in Remote whose
# every hit curation blocks and the down Remote returns nothing, so it
# answers 503 (#5495), not an empty 200. Red on main before the fix
# (artifact-keeper 1.13.0).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats client.composer"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="4951 6285 6332"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
